  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 150 PM MST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nThanksgiving...The next shortwave trough aloft moves from eastern \nMontana and eastern Wyoming in the morning, to the western high \nplains by evening. This system is moisture starved with only perhaps \nsome mid and high level cloudiness. Low and mid level gradients \nsuggest a breezy to windy day. More mild downwind of the Laramie \nRange and I-25 due to downslope warming. Continued cold to the west \nof I-25.\n\nFriday...Looks like the beginning of a windy weekend with strong \nnorthwest flow aloft and deep unidirectional flow in the atmosphere. \nWill likely see high winds for our typically wind prone locations \nsuch as Arlington, Bordeaux and the I-80 Summit, with strong winds \npossibly in nearby locations of southeast Wyoming as well. Enough \nlow and mid level moisture for orographic snows across the Snowy and \nSierra Madre Ranges. Despite the winds, it will remain relatively \nmild with 700 mb temperatures near -4 Celsius yielding high \ntemperatures in the 40s west of I-25, with low to mid 50s east of I-\n25.\n\nSaturday...Strong west northwest flow will occur in the low and mid \nlevels, and looking like a more widespread high wind event for much \nof southeast Wyoming and parts of the Nebraska Panhandle. Again, \nlooks like adequate mid level moisture for orographic snows across \nthe northern Laramie, Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges. Will see a slow \ncooling trend over the weekend based on 700 mb temperatures.\n\nSunday...The flow aloft turns westerly though still remains strong \nenough at low and mid levels for windy conditions across the wind \nprone locations. A surface high across the central Plains states \nwill slide across our eastern counties, to the east of I-25, with \nwinds lessening. \n\nMonday...A fast moving shortwave trough aloft will sweep eastward \nacross our counties, and with adequate mid level moisture, will \nproduce orographic snows for our Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges. \nTemperatures similar to Sunday, in the 40s west of I-25, with upper \n40s to mid 50s further east.",
